{% comment %}
  Global app-embed counterpart to deposit-notice.liquid. That block only
  shows up once a merchant manually adds it to a specific section/template;
  this one shows up as a single on/off switch in the theme editor's
  "App embeds" panel (Online Store > Customize > App embeds) and, once
  switched on, applies to every theme the merchant uses it on with no
  further setup. Both ship side by side on purpose - this is the easy
  default, deposit-notice.liquid stays for merchants who want the notice in
  one exact spot within a specific section instead.

  Reads the same $app:pfand metafield the section block does, and for the
  same reason has to use the bracketed "$app" form rather than dot syntax -
  see that file's comment.

  Guarded on `product` because an app embed's Liquid runs on every storefront
  page once enabled, not just product pages - `enabled_on.templates` below
  keeps Shopify from even attempting to render this outside the product
  template, but the guard stays as defense in depth.
{% endcomment %}
{% if product %}
  {% assign pfand = product.metafields["$app"].pfand %}
  {% if pfand.value %}
    {%- assign deposit_amount = pfand.value | money -%}
    {{ 'deposit-notice-embed.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    <p id="pfandlock-deposit-embed" hidden>
      {{ 'deposit_notice.text' | t: amount: deposit_amount }}
    </p>
    <script src="{{ 'deposit-notice-embed.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Pfandlock deposit notice",
  "target": "body",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
